<<~ ahu #/contract>>

!! Deserializer — Contract

TW5 `module-type = "tiddlerdeserializer"` module keyed to `text/memetic-wikitext`.

When TW5 encounters a tiddler with that content-type, it calls:

```
deserializer(text: string, fields: Record<string, unknown>) → TiddlerFields[]
```

Carrier model — one file, one carrier (`memetic-wikitext-framing#/frame-security`):
* ''Framed'': the live heading opens the carrier and the span reader (`readFrame`) closes it; it becomes `[parent, ...children]`, with the prologue and postamble as carriage records under the parent.
* ''Torn'' (no ETX after STX, a second heading or text frame, a mark out of spine order): held verbatim as ONE `text/plain` record carrying `$torn`; the Confluence gate refuses it.
* ''Bare body'' (no SOH framing): treated as a single carrier with `fields.title` as URI.
* A stream of carriers belongs to the SYN-framed profile, never to this deserializer.

Parent tiddler: `text = original carrier text`, `type = "text/memetic-wikitext+tiddlywiki"`.
Child tiddlers (ahu slots): `text = ahu body text`, also `type = "text/memetic-wikitext+tiddlywiki"`.
No AST→string reconstruction. MemeticParser owns all rendering for both levels.

Compiled artifact: `packages/lararium-tw5/tiddlers/src/memetic-wikitext-deserializer.js`
Build: `pnpm --filter @lararium/tw5 build:plugin`

